Z||000002||Old Lar||10-09-2001||09:33 PM||||For batter acceleration anything you do to the 2.5 L four will encrease the HP from 92 to 100.  You won't notice a thing.  Put in 4.10 gears you'd get batter acceleration.<P>Education is  somthing terrible to waste on the illiterate.||||reg||1
Z||000003||erikred||10-11-2001||10:00 AM||||Start by tuning your car. Get some decent (not overpriced) spark plugs, gap em properly. Install some spiral core low resistance plug wires. Get a new brass terminal dist. cap. Play around with the ignition timming. Install a high flow air filter such as a K&N.<P>After that you will have to go to bolt ons. Holley sells an improved TBI that is a direct replacement (over $300). GM sells performance intake manifolds ($215) and so does Clifford ($even more expensive). You will need to make a simple adapter plate for them as they are setup for a carb, or you could just use a carb, it would be cheaper. Hooker sells a header (under $300). You may notice improve throtle respons with an MSD unit and coil ($130 6A)(less than $50 for coil). The thing you will notice most is changing the cam ($200-$300). Be sure to use metal gears if you do that ($70). <BR> <A HREF="http://www.amotion.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amotion.com/</A>  is a good site for parts and performance info. go to the pontiac 4cyl section and then to the parts selection guide. It gives a guidline of what cam to use with what engine combo and how much power to expect. According to them the combo above can give 130-150 hp depending on your compression ratio. That would be as good or faster than a v6 fiero.<P>Check my answers to your question about turbo 4cyl. for more info.<P>Erik-<p>[This message has been edited by erikred (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||14
